  "worked_solution": "Two lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nNow, let's examine the direction of the sides in the figure to determine whether any pair lies along parallel lines.\n\nNotice that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ both lie along horizontal lines. The remaining sides have different directions, so they do not form any additional pair of parallel sides.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/7f55b88378fe0e9389ea7a540cc40a02c9e619854a6815e9700b808770fa3a13.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ are parallel. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{DE}\n$$",
